== the generation rules (mutants_of() directly, no build)
ok   a unary & is not an op mutant
ok   a binary & is still an op mutant
ok   a dereference/declarator * is not an op mutant
ok   a binary * is still an op mutant
ok   a unary - after return is not an op mutant
ok   a binary - is still an op mutant
ok   && is mutated only by logic, to ||
ok   || is mutated only by logic, to &&
ok   -> is never split into a - mutant
ok   gcd_lcm renames my_gcd to my_lcm when my_lcm is declared
ok   gcd_lcm drops the rename when nothing declares my_lcm
ok   swap_args of a 3-argument call keeps the first argument fixed
ok   swap_args of a 2-argument call exchanges both
ok   status turns ADF_UNSUPPORTED into ADF_OK
ok   status turns ADF_OK into ADF_DOMAIN
ok   drop_call removes a bare call statement
ok   drop_call excludes _init and _clear
ok   call_swap renames my_add to my_sub when my_sub is declared
ok   call_swap drops the rename when nothing declares my_sub
ok   prec replaces the argument with 2
ok   prec leaves the parameter declaration alone
